{"step_index":903,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:38:10Z","content":"### 1. Dynamic Case Resolution in the Auditor\n\nThe 7-card auditor in [scripts/audit_day_cards.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/scripts/audit_day_cards.py) is **100% dynamic**:\n\n* It does not hardcode case assumptions.\n* For any target date, it invokes `engine.resolve_general_case(context)` to compute the exact canonical case based on rank, season, tone, and collision rules.\n* It displays the dynamically resolved case in the audit report:\n  * August 24, 2026 ➔ dynamically resolved as **`[CASE_02]`** (Simple Saint on Weekday)\n  * August 23, 2026 ➔ dynamically resolved as **`[CASE_19]`** (Afterfeast / Polyeleos collision on Sunday)\n\n```\n=======================================================\n 7-CARD DAY AUDIT REPORT: 2026-08-24 [CASE_02]\n Overall Status: PASS (7/7 cards passed)\n=======================================================\n[PASS] General Info\n[PASS] Daily/Great Vespers\n[PASS] Small/Great Compline\n[PASS] Midnight Office\n[PASS] Daily/Great Matins\n[PASS] The Hours\n[PASS] Divine Liturgy\n=======================================================\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Canonical Terminology Clarification\n\nIn our **2010 Lviv Typikon** codebase, the standardized, immutable terminology is:\n\n* **\"Canonical Case\"** or **\"Dolnytsky Paradigm\"** (e.g., `CASE_01` to `CASE_20` in [02a_logic_general.json](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/json_db/02a_logic_general.json) and `CASE_21` to `CASE_26` in `02c_logic_triodion.json`).\n* In [Data/services_cases_logic.txt](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/Data/services_cases_logic.txt) and [.agents/references/liturgical_authority.md](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/.agents/references/liturgical_authority.md), they are codified as the **\"Dolnytsky Paradigms\" / \"Liturgical Cases\"**.\n\nWe will strictly and exclusively use the term **\"Canonical Case\"** or **\"Paradigm\"** across all reports, code, and documentation.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Verification & Compliance\n* **Compliance & AST Linter**: `pytest tests/test_session_compliance.py tests/test_anti_pattern_ast.py` passed (**4 passed in 0.87s**).\n* **Automated Day Auditor**: Successfully audited dates across weekday and Sunday paradigms with full 7-card validation.\n\n---\n### Summary of Work\n* Integrated dynamic `resolve_general_case(context)` resolution into [scripts/audit_day_cards.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/scripts/audit_day_cards.py).\n* Standardized all terminology on **Canonical Case / Dolnytsky Paradigm**.\n* Verified dynamic case resolution on August 24 (`CASE_02`) and August 23 (`CASE_19`) with all 7 cards passing."}
