{"step_index":911,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:39:24Z","content":"### How We Prevent the \"Sample-to-Universal\" Hallucination\n\nThe only mathematically sound way to prevent an AI from hallucinating that a few passing samples represent a complete dataset is **Brute-Force 365-Day Exhaustive Execution**.\n\nWe just ran the new automated 365-day sweep in [scripts/audit_day_cards.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/scripts/audit_day_cards.py#L150-L200) across all **2,555 cards** of the year 2026:\n\n```powershell\n.venv\\Scripts\\python scripts/audit_day_cards.py --all-year\n```\n\n---\n\n### Empirical Proof: The 365-Day Reality vs. The 1-Day Sample\n\n```\n=======================================================\n EXHAUSTIVE 365-DAY 7-CARD AUDIT SWEEP: 2026\n Total Days to Audit: 365 (2,555 Total Cards)\n=======================================================\n Passed Days: 280/365 (76.7%)\n Failed Days: 85/365\n=======================================================\n```\n\nTesting only August 24 gave a false sense of completion (`100%`). The full 365-day sweep immediately exposed that **85 days (23.3%) currently fail**:\n\n1. **Vigil Paradigms (Cases 07, 09, 10 — e.g., Jan 1, Jan 6, Jan 30)**:\n   * Compline & Midnight Office omission/replacement rules during All-Night Vigils need explicit handling in the card validator.\n2. **Theophany Eve & Fast Days (e.g., Jan 5)**:\n   * Vesperal Liturgy of St. Basil has missing Troparia & Kontakia sequences in Card 7.\n3. **Forefeast / Afterfeast Saturday Collisions (Case 20 — e.g., Jan 14)**:\n   * `resolve_vespers_stichera` has an unresolved `logic_switch` branch for `CASE_20` returning an empty distribution list.\n\n---\n\n### The 4-Pillar Programmatic Defense\n\n1. **Zero Sample Extrapolation**: An AI is programmatically forbidden from asserting completion unless `audit_day_cards.py --all-year` outputs `365/365 Passed (100%)`.\n2. **Automated AST Anti-Pattern Linter**: [tests/test_anti_pattern_ast.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/tests/test_anti_pattern_ast.py) physically blocks any hardcoded dates or static string returns.\n3. **Deterministic Failure Logging**: Every failing date among the 85 is captured with its exact `CASE_ID`, failing card name, and missing element.\n4. **Iterative Convergence to 365/365**: We systematically fix each category of the 85 failures (e.g. Case 20 stichera, Vigil card suppression, Vesperal Liturgy sequences) until the 365-day pass count reaches **365/365 (100%)**.\n\n---\n### Summary of Work\n* Added the `--all-year` batch sweep to [scripts/audit_day_cards.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/scripts/audit_day_cards.py).\n* Ran the exhaustive sweep across all 365 days (2,555 cards) of 2026: **280 passed (76.7%), 85 failed (23.3%)**.\n* Cataloged the 3 major clusters among the 85 failures for systematic root-cause resolution.","thinking":"**Analyzing the Sweep Results**\n\nThe 365-day sweep's results are in, and they're revealing. We're at 280 successful days, which is roughly 76.7% of the total, but 85 days failed. I'm focusing on those failures now, with particular attention to Vigil days, and their patterns.\n\n\n"}
